{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "factor x^2 - 1\n  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)\n  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)\n  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "factor", "ucas": "factor x^2-1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "factor", "input": "x^2 - 1", "result": "(x - 1)*(x + 1)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "normal_form", "passed": true, "text": "both sides have the same normal form"}], "proof": {"kind": "symbolic", "text": "both sides have the same normal form over Q"}, "files": [], "text": "factor x^2 - 1\n  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)\n  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)\n  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "gcd x^4 - 1, x^3 - 1\n  = x - 1\n  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime\n  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "gcd", "ucas": "gcd x^4-1, x^3-1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "gcd", "p": "x^4 - 1", "q": "x^3 - 1", "result": "x - 1"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "exact_division", "passed": true, "text": "divides both, cofactors coprime"}], "proof": {"kind": "symbolic", "text": "exact division"}, "files": [], "text": "gcd x^4 - 1, x^3 - 1\n  = x - 1\n  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime\n  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "phi(12) = 4\n  how: 12 = 2^2 * 3; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2^1*1 * 2\n  the order of the unit group (Z/12)*; lambda(12) = 2 is its exponent\n  check: counted the k in 1..12 with gcd(k, 12) = 1: 4\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "phi", "ucas": "phi 12", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "phi", "method": "12 = 2^2 * 3; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2^1*1 * 2", "lhs": "phi(12)", "value": "4", "value_int": 4, "headline": "phi(12) = 4", "details": ["the order of the unit group (Z/12)*; lambda(12) = 2 is its exponent"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "counted the k in 1..12 with gcd(k, 12) = 1: 4"}], "files": [], "text": "phi(12) = 4\n  how: 12 = 2^2 * 3; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2^1*1 * 2\n  the order of the unit group (Z/12)*; lambda(12) = 2 is its exponent\n  check: counted the k in 1..12 with gcd(k, 12) = 1: 4\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "3^-1 = 4 mod 11\n  how: extended Euclid: 4*3 - 1*11 = 1\n  check: 3 * 4 = 12 = 1*11 + 1\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "inverse_mod", "ucas": "inverse 3 mod 11", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "inverse", "method": "extended Euclid: 4*3 - 1*11 = 1", "lhs": "3^-1", "modulus": "11", "value": "4", "value_int": 4, "headline": "3^-1 = 4 mod 11"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "3 * 4 = 12 = 1*11 + 1"}], "files": [], "text": "3^-1 = 4 mod 11\n  how: extended Euclid: 4*3 - 1*11 = 1\n  check: 3 * 4 = 12 = 1*11 + 1\n"}, "isError": false}}
